        ],
        "abstract": "Semiconductor manufacturing faces growing challenges as the demand for smaller, faster, and more efficient chips intensifies. This paper investigates the application of artificial intelligence (AI) in transforming production and design processes within the semiconductor industry. AI-driven techniques enhance defect detection by 30% and increase wafer yields by 15% through real-time process adjustments. In design, AI accelerates computer-aided workflowsimproving verification, layout optimization, and predictive simulationsto reduce design cycles by up to 30%. Despite challenges such as high infrastructure costs and complex validation, AI proves indispensable for managing billions of transistors with nanoscale precision. Case studies and industry data underscore AI's potential to enhance efficiency, reduce costs, and drive innovation in semiconductor manufacturing and design.",
